\name{sdev}
\alias{sdev}
\title{Calculates a standard-deviation quantity used by the simulation code}

\description{
Calculates a standard-deviation quantity used by the simulation code.
}

\usage{
sdev(x, na.rm = FALSE)
}

\arguments{
   \item{x}{Input object.}
   \item{na.rm}{Function argument used by this operation.}
}
\value{
A numeric standard-deviation result. For a matrix or data frame, a numeric vector is returned with one standard deviation per column; for a vector or other object coerced to a vector, a numeric scalar is returned.
}
